# Copy to the client repo root as `.dockerignore`.
# Everything here stays out of the build context. This is a security control as
# much as a speed one: .env and .git are the two things you most want to never
# accidentally bake into a layer that gets pushed to a registry.

.git
.github
.gitignore
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
.next
dist
build
coverage
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
